{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R6niVxjbcqLKZRrPyq6nxs","type":"tool_result","content":"R04 {\"gate\": \"G2\", \"title\": \"Retrieval-corpus integrity\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Memory entries poisoned or shared across tenants\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieved chunks not checked for size, type, or hidden instructions\", \"owner\": \"R01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Embedding or reranker model swapped without review\", \"owner\": \"C05\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no retrieval corpus or search index.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R04.1\", \"check\": \"Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\"}, {\"id\": \"R04.2\", \"check\": \"Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.\"}, {\"id\": \"R04.3\", \"check\": \"Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens\nR05 {\"gate\": \"G3\", \"title\": \"Memory isolation and write validation\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"Separate memory by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed. Block access across those lines unless it is clearly approved. Check what gets written to memory. Test that one poisoned run can't quietly plant instructions in another run's memory. Don't move the agent's own output into trusted memory without review, and let unverified entries expire. Write checks must also cover content that arrives through ordinary queries, not just special write paths.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"No record of who wrote a memory entry, or no way to remove it\", \"owner\": \"R06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieval search not filtered by the requesting tenant\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Rollback restoring old memory or index state unchecked\", \"owner\": \"C07\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no memory that lasts between runs.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R05.1\", \"check\": \"Memory reads and writes are scoped by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed, and cross-scope access is denied unless explicitly allowed.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find memory read and write code (`memory`, `store`, `namespace`, keys). 2) Check keys include tenant, agent type, instance, or task as needed. 3) Answer no if keys omit tenant, the scope comes from a model argument, or reads fall back to a shared or global namespace.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.2\", \"check\": \"Every memory write, including content arriving through ordinary queries, passes validation before it is stored.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) List every memory write path, including automatic saves from ordinary conversation. 2) Check each passes validation before storing. 3) Answer no if any path writes without validation, or validation errors are caught and the write continues.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.3\", \"check\": \"The agent's own output cannot reach trusted or shared memory without a review step.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where agent output is written to shared or trusted memory. 2) Check a review step gates the write. 3) Answer no if agent output goes straight into shared or trusted memory, or the review flag defaults to approved.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.4\", \"check\": \"Unverified entries have an expiry that is enforced.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how unverified entries are marked and expired (`ttl`\nR06 {\"gate\": \"G3\", \"title\": \"Memory provenance and cleanup\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"For any memory entry, look up who wrote it, when, for which task, from what input, and the context size at the time. Show that you can find, quarantine, and remove bad entries, and control their reuse in later sessions.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Memory not separated by tenant, agent type, instance, or task\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Poisoned retrieval documents not quarantined or expired\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Context size not logged for each action decision\", \"owner\": \"R07\"}, {\"problem\": \"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded\", \"owner\": \"A06\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no memory that lasts between runs.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R06.1\", \"check\": \"Each memory entry stores its writer, time, task, source input, and context size at write time.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the memory entry schema. 2) Check fields for writer, time, task, source input, and context size. 3) Answer no if any is missing, or set only on some write paths.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.2\", \"check\": \"Derived entries such as summaries keep links to the entries they came from.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find summary or derived-entry creation code. 2) Check it stores links to source entry IDs. 3) Answer no if derived entries keep no source links.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.3\", \"check\": \"Code can find entries by source or writer and quarantine or delete them, along with derived entries and caches.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find code that queries by source or writer and quarantines or deletes. 2) Check it also handles derived entries and caches. 3) Answer no if lookup by source or writer is impossible, or derived entries and caches are left in place.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.4\", \"check\": \"Quarantined or deleted entries are excluded from retrieval in later sessions.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find memory retrieval code. 2) Check it excludes quarantined or deleted entries in new sessions. 3) Answer no if retrieval ignores the quarantine flag, or a cache or index still returns removed entries.\"}]}\nR07 {\"gate\": \"G2\", \"title\": \"Decision-time context size\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"For each action, log how full the model's context was when it decided, in tokens. Document how you count. Say whether each value was measured, estimated, or unavailable. Cover cached input, compaction (shrinking the context), and limits the provider hides. Per-call billing totals don't automatically equal context size. Use them only if your counting method shows they match. A missing value is a clear gap, never zero. Check that the value survives tool handoffs and can be searched next to the action's identity and result. See the [telemetry conventions](otel-conventions.md).\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Behavior not compared across context-size ranges\", \"owner\": \"R09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Token or cost limits not enforced outside the model\", \"owner\": \"B07\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R07.1\", \"check\": \"Each action record includes the model's context size in tokens at decision time.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"inventory_kinds\": [\"model_call\", \"audit_write\"], \"verify\": \"1) Inventory every model call, including classifiers and helpers, and every action/audit write. 2) Trace available decision-time context into each record. 3) Answer no when an available measure is dropped; NULL/unavailable is not permission to omit a value that exists. Do not exclude routing decisions or delegate start/result events merely by calling them lifecycle events.\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.2\", \"check\": \"Each value is labeled measured, estimated, or unavailable, and a missing value is stored as unknown, never as zero.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where context size is recorded. 2) Check a label of measured, estimated, or unavailable, and how missing values are stored. 3) Answer no if there is no label, or a missing value defaults to `0` (`or 0`, `?? 0`, `.get(..., 0)`).\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.3\", \"check\": \"The count comes from a stated method that handles cached input and compaction, not a copied per-call billing total.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how context size is counted. 2) Check a stated method covers cached input and compaction. 3) Answer no if it copies `usage.input_tokens` or a billing total with no stated method that matches it, or ignores cache and compaction.\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.4\", \"check\": \"The value is carried across tool handoffs and stored with the action's identi\n5:python review_coverage.py ledger FINDINGS.json CHECK --rows rows.json --attempts attempts.json\n79:        result['attempt_categories'] = ATTEMPTS[cid]\n84:    \"\"\"Validate a positive claim, including candidate coverage and bypass attempts.\"\"\"\n122:    attempts = c.get('attempts', [])\n123:    if not isinstance(attempts, list):\n124:        return errors + ['attempts must be a list']\n126:    for attempt in attempts:\n127:        if not isinstance(attempt, dict):\n128:            errors.append('attempts must be objects')\n130:        if isinstance(attempt.get('category'), str):\n131:            categories.add(attempt['category'])\n132:        if (attempt.get('outcome') not in ('blocked', 'not_applicable') or not attempt.get('input')\n133:                or len(norm(attempt.get('trace', '')).split()) < 8\n134:                or not quote_found(repo, attempt.get('evidence'), attempt.get('quote'))):\n135:            errors.append('attempt needs concrete input, quoted code and traced blocked/exempt outcome; accepted/unresolved cannot hold')\n136:    if set(meta.get('attempt_categories', [])) - categories:\n137:        errors.append('needs falsification attempts: ' + ', '.join(sorted(set(meta['attempt_categories']) - categories)))\n143:    lists = {k: c.get(k) if isinstance(c.get(k),list) else [] for k in ('coverage','deviations','attempts')}\n146:    rows += [r for r in lists['attempts'] if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get('outcome') in ('accepted', 'unclear')]\n156:    record.add_argument('--rows', required=True); record.add_argument('--attempts'); record.add_argument('--deviations')\n173:    for option, field in ((args.rows, 'coverage'), (args.attempts, 'attempts'), (args.deviations, 'deviations')):","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19886412-4462-40d7-a3aa-0b2fc484d614","uuid":"71502df9-78bc-4d0c-85f1-ced9b2da4abe","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:37:52.888Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"R04 {\"gate\": \"G2\", \"title\": \"Retrieval-corpus integrity\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Memory entries poisoned or shared across tenants\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieved chunks not checked for size, type, or hidden instructions\", \"owner\": \"R01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Embedding or reranker model swapped without review\", \"owner\": \"C05\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no retrieval corpus or search index.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R04.1\", \"check\": \"Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\"}, {\"id\": \"R04.2\", \"check\": \"Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.\"}, {\"id\": \"R04.3\", \"check\": \"Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens\nR05 {\"gate\": \"G3\", \"title\": \"Memory isolation and write validation\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"Separate memory by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed. Block access across those lines unless it is clearly approved. Check what gets written to memory. Test that one poisoned run can't quietly plant instructions in another run's memory. Don't move the agent's own output into trusted memory without review, and let unverified entries expire. Write checks must also cover content that arrives through ordinary queries, not just special write paths.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"No record of who wrote a memory entry, or no way to remove it\", \"owner\": \"R06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieval search not filtered by the requesting tenant\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Rollback restoring old memory or index state unchecked\", \"owner\": \"C07\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no memory that lasts between runs.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R05.1\", \"check\": \"Memory reads and writes are scoped by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed, and cross-scope access is denied unless explicitly allowed.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find memory read and write code (`memory`, `store`, `namespace`, keys). 2) Check keys include tenant, agent type, instance, or task as needed. 3) Answer no if keys omit tenant, the scope comes from a model argument, or reads fall back to a shared or global namespace.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.2\", \"check\": \"Every memory write, including content arriving through ordinary queries, passes validation before it is stored.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) List every memory write path, including automatic saves from ordinary conversation. 2) Check each passes validation before storing. 3) Answer no if any path writes without validation, or validation errors are caught and the write continues.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.3\", \"check\": \"The agent's own output cannot reach trusted or shared memory without a review step.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where agent output is written to shared or trusted memory. 2) Check a review step gates the write. 3) Answer no if agent output goes straight into shared or trusted memory, or the review flag defaults to approved.\"}, {\"id\": \"R05.4\", \"check\": \"Unverified entries have an expiry that is enforced.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how unverified entries are marked and expired (`ttl`\nR06 {\"gate\": \"G3\", \"title\": \"Memory provenance and cleanup\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"For any memory entry, look up who wrote it, when, for which task, from what input, and the context size at the time. Show that you can find, quarantine, and remove bad entries, and control their reuse in later sessions.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Memory not separated by tenant, agent type, instance, or task\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Poisoned retrieval documents not quarantined or expired\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Context size not logged for each action decision\", \"owner\": \"R07\"}, {\"problem\": \"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded\", \"owner\": \"A06\"}], \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no memory that lasts between runs.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R06.1\", \"check\": \"Each memory entry stores its writer, time, task, source input, and context size at write time.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the memory entry schema. 2) Check fields for writer, time, task, source input, and context size. 3) Answer no if any is missing, or set only on some write paths.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.2\", \"check\": \"Derived entries such as summaries keep links to the entries they came from.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find summary or derived-entry creation code. 2) Check it stores links to source entry IDs. 3) Answer no if derived entries keep no source links.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.3\", \"check\": \"Code can find entries by source or writer and quarantine or delete them, along with derived entries and caches.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find code that queries by source or writer and quarantines or deletes. 2) Check it also handles derived entries and caches. 3) Answer no if lookup by source or writer is impossible, or derived entries and caches are left in place.\"}, {\"id\": \"R06.4\", \"check\": \"Quarantined or deleted entries are excluded from retrieval in later sessions.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find memory retrieval code. 2) Check it excludes quarantined or deleted entries in new sessions. 3) Answer no if retrieval ignores the quarantine flag, or a cache or index still returns removed entries.\"}]}\nR07 {\"gate\": \"G2\", \"title\": \"Decision-time context size\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"For each action, log how full the model's context was when it decided, in tokens. Document how you count. Say whether each value was measured, estimated, or unavailable. Cover cached input, compaction (shrinking the context), and limits the provider hides. Per-call billing totals don't automatically equal context size. Use them only if your counting method shows they match. A missing value is a clear gap, never zero. Check that the value survives tool handoffs and can be searched next to the action's identity and result. See the [telemetry conventions](otel-conventions.md).\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Behavior not compared across context-size ranges\", \"owner\": \"R09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Token or cost limits not enforced outside the model\", \"owner\": \"B07\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R07.1\", \"check\": \"Each action record includes the model's context size in tokens at decision time.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"inventory_kinds\": [\"model_call\", \"audit_write\"], \"verify\": \"1) Inventory every model call, including classifiers and helpers, and every action/audit write. 2) Trace available decision-time context into each record. 3) Answer no when an available measure is dropped; NULL/unavailable is not permission to omit a value that exists. Do not exclude routing decisions or delegate start/result events merely by calling them lifecycle events.\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.2\", \"check\": \"Each value is labeled measured, estimated, or unavailable, and a missing value is stored as unknown, never as zero.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where context size is recorded. 2) Check a label of measured, estimated, or unavailable, and how missing values are stored. 3) Answer no if there is no label, or a missing value defaults to `0` (`or 0`, `?? 0`, `.get(..., 0)`).\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.3\", \"check\": \"The count comes from a stated method that handles cached input and compaction, not a copied per-call billing total.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how context size is counted. 2) Check a stated method covers cached input and compaction. 3) Answer no if it copies `usage.input_tokens` or a billing total with no stated method that matches it, or ignores cache and compaction.\"}, {\"id\": \"R07.4\", \"check\": \"The value is carried across tool handoffs and stored with the action's identi\n5:python review_coverage.py ledger FINDINGS.json CHECK --rows rows.json --attempts attempts.json\n79:        result['attempt_categories'] = ATTEMPTS[cid]\n84:    \"\"\"Validate a positive claim, including candidate coverage and bypass attempts.\"\"\"\n122:    attempts = c.get('attempts', [])\n123:    if not isinstance(attempts, list):\n124:        return errors + ['attempts must be a list']\n126:    for attempt in attempts:\n127:        if not isinstance(attempt, dict):\n128:            errors.append('attempts must be objects')\n130:        if isinstance(attempt.get('category'), str):\n131:            categories.add(attempt['category'])\n132:        if (attempt.get('outcome') not in ('blocked', 'not_applicable') or not attempt.get('input')\n133:                or len(norm(attempt.get('trace', '')).split()) < 8\n134:                or not quote_found(repo, attempt.get('evidence'), attempt.get('quote'))):\n135:            errors.append('attempt needs concrete input, quoted code and traced blocked/exempt outcome; accepted/unresolved cannot hold')\n136:    if set(meta.get('attempt_categories', [])) - categories:\n137:        errors.append('needs falsification attempts: ' + ', '.join(sorted(set(meta['attempt_categories']) - categories)))\n143:    lists = {k: c.get(k) if isinstance(c.get(k),list) else [] for k in ('coverage','deviations','attempts')}\n146:    rows += [r for r in lists['attempts'] if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get('outcome') in ('accepted', 'unclear')]\n156:    record.add_argument('--rows', required=True); record.add_argument('--attempts'); record.add_argument('--deviations')\n173:    for option, field in ((args.rows, 'coverage'), (args.attempts, 'attempts'), (args.deviations, 'deviations')):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R6niVxjbcqLKZRrPyq6nxs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
