{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDfJHjMqrfVcNcUHd6mW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review of R04–R08 is finished and saved to `agent/brace-findings.json`. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch R04,R05,R06,R07,R08 --before-challenges` printed `Valid. gap: 4, needs_evidence: 1`. I didn't run challenges, as instructed. The file holds only these five items, in normal mode. I didn't execute any of the repo's code.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| R04 | gap | `ingest.py:122` takes `business_unit` from the payload with no named-source check. Documents have no trust-level or access-permission fields. Nothing expires, revokes or later quarantines an accepted document. R04.3 is `yes`: `read_document` filters by tenant in SQL (`documents.py:24`). |\n| R05 | gap | `memory_read` uses a model-supplied `business_unit` (`memory.py:44`), so the model can read another tenant's notes. R05.2–R05.4 are `yes`: writes are validated, stored unverified, and expire after 30 days, enforced on read. |\n| R06 | gap | The source input (`source_doc_id`) is optional and supplied by the model (`memory.py:94`). R06.2 and R06.3 are `unknown`: no derived-entry or find/quarantine code is in the repo. R06.4 is `yes`. |\n| R07 | gap | The extractor's `subagent_started` and `subagent_finished` audit rows (`extractor.py:51` and `:88`) omit the context size, which is available at that point. The parent-to-child handoff (`documents.py:36`) doesn't pass it either. R07.2 and R07.3 are `yes`. |\n| R08 | needs_evidence | No detection rules or alert routing are in the repo, so all three checks are `unknown`. Denied calls are logged, so rules could be built on them. |\n\n- **Prescan hits:** I dismissed H006 and H007, the two R05 hits. Both are `lru_cache` on config, not tenant data. The other five hits belong to B07–B11, outside this batch.\n- **Coverage ledgers:** the ledgers for every `yes` are in the findings file, with falsification attempts where the policy required them.\n- **Weak spots:** R05.2's note filter is a regex denylist that a paraphrase could evade. R04 treats the `documents` table as the retrieval corpus, since the repo has no search index.\n- **Scratch files:** `brace-prescan.json`, `brace-inventory.json`, and my scratch files in `ledgers/` are left in the workspace."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":946,"cache_read_input_tokens":84114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":946},"output_tokens":791,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19886412-4462-40d7-a3aa-0b2fc484d614","uuid":"40c25450-8566-48dd-af5a-7dcff054db65","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:39:20.817Z","request_id":"req_011CgDfJHHLFMaKEfP9VB1D2"}
